    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "\"In 1968 César\nestablished himself as the modern demigod of polyurethane,\nthe inspired pioneer of industrial chemistry.\" \"The\nworld's most celebrated modern art museums are proud today\nto boast expansions by César among their collections.\nThese mounds of brightly coloured solid foam have the definitive\nbeauty of organically free forms, and their occupation\nof space is the pure and simple result of a chemical process\ncarried to completion.\"",
      "links": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Pierre Restany: \"César and the\npoetry of industrial chemistry.\" Domus 462\n(August 1968)",
      "links": []
    }
